Z||000000||mrgone||06-12-2001||03:08 AM||||???   my parents had an old full size dodge ram charger, yellow, raised up, sheep wool seats and the roof came off (one like in the choclair lets ride video)  <P>those would be FUN! now why dont they make trucks like that anymore? i wish removable truck roofs,removable sunroofs, targa tops, and t roofs were more popular for options on cars<P>and the nissan pulsar with t roofs and a removable hatch!? man.. beach mobile. <P>if my buddy in highschool didnt have an 87 pulsar nx with t tops and trunk off, i dont think i would be into fieros.<P>i want to design cars someday.... fun is ingredient #1. (saftey is up there too)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||06-12-2001||10:20 AM||||probaly leakage has some to do with it. seems more often than not anyone who has had a t top car of any kind (myself included) has had some problem with the tops leaking. <P>those big blazers and broncos with the removable tops are real popular now. seems like to big and bulky a thing to be messing with though. my next attempt at an open air car will hopefully be a full on convertable.||||reg||1
Z||000002||c m west||06-12-2001||11:49 AM||||Our Support Vehicle here at West Coast Fiero is a 1991 Chevy K5 Blazer. I had this truck since high school and it has had its share of miss-uses, inside and out - its a total shaggin'-wagon. There are several reasons that removable tops are no longer produced, such as leakage, cost effectiveness, and the simple fact that people were no longer removing them - and even if they did take them off, where would they put the shell. My Blazer has its top off more often than not, and is often seen cruising down sunset with the top off, with the party in the back<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero||||reg||1
